On Sun, 2013-08-04, tedav wrote:
> Personally, I have always felt that Rodney's harassment of players that reach demigod status should be more interesting.
>
> Right now, every rn1(200, 50) [allmain.c#267] turns
> there is a 
> 1/3 chance of nothing
> 1/6 chance of curse items
> 1/6 chance of summon nasties
> 1/6 chance of aggravate monsters
> 1/6 chance of Summon Wizard
>
> Thing is, this can get a bit repetitive, and doesn't really feel
> like the Rodney is throwing everything he's got at you.
>
> I propose a few changes.
>
> 1) The intervene() timer should be impacted by luck.
> Low luck should both increase the average frequency and increase the unpredictability of the harassment.
> This is just an initial proposal but something like rn1((200-Luck), 65-rnl(40))
> seems a bit more appropriate. 

Isn't the poor unlucky player suffering enough already?  I don't know
what a late game with low luck feels like.

And that's part of the problem with the proposal: doesn't everyone
have extreme luck from the midgame onwards?  Seems to me this would
affect very few games, and those games would already behave in unusual
ways due to low luck?

> 2) Expanded list of possible effects:
[snip the existing ones]

> *drop boulders all around the < 

> *darken much of the level and remove fuel from light sources the
> player is carrying

This one could be very nice, I think.  It would add to the paranoia in
a new way: Rodney cannot just affect *you*, but the dungeon itself.

Or perhaps Darkness should be a general monster spell?  Something e.g.
a lich could cast?

The "darkening part of the level" part is what I like. Removing fuel
from light sources ... not sure about that, and anyway my light source
tends to be a magic lamp or Sunsword.

